WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:10.000
Blue spheres represent water. Gold spheres represent dissolved sugar.
Water is the solvent; sugar is a solute.

00:10.000 --> 00:20.000
In this model, water can cross the membrane. Sugar cannot.
Partially permeable means only some particles pass through.

00:20.000 --> 00:30.000
Water crosses both ways, but more moves towards the concentrated side.
Net movement is the difference between the opposing flows.

00:30.000 --> 00:40.000
At equal concentrations, water keeps moving both ways at equal rates overall.
There is no net movement. Particles have not stopped.

00:40.000 --> 00:50.000
In dilute surroundings, water enters cells through their membranes.
A plant wall resists expansion. An animal cell may swell and burst.

00:50.000 --> 00:55.000
Put a cell in a more concentrated solution.
Pause and predict: which way does water move?

00:55.000 --> 01:00.000
Water leaves overall. The cell loses water and shrinks.
